#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068619 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068779 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4640f978-9caa-5960-bec4-f153a1b4cc5d" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d86c6bd2-e528-55ed-bbfc-9f5ecbec024e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5924" :question/problem "Graph the function $y = -\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1.$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $y = -\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/9d/9da0db2e6c97e507e82b7ca801e46802fabf91ad31ff53ad3cc9ae580151370a.png)\n\n- Translate it by one unit to the right to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x-1}.$ \n\n![](images/8c/8ce8c53f202f04b3b34a247b797f65f7616e8772afa1751de126ddd401417bd7.png)\n\nNotice that the vertical asymptote is now $x=1.$\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{2}{x-1}.$\n\n![](images/c9/c9b708a20d9c6c12f0016279e8d7a3ea55597e7645f0a9518f1c32e8a8406e47.png)\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit down to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1.$ \n\n![](images/e1/e100b552adb71cae1295492a58b0e60525813adb87d9815ba64a151a856f0c46.png)\n\nNotice that the horizontal asymptote is now $y=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068620 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "308f3685-0a90-56f3-9653-a83cec4286d2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Some Unknowns Given the Graph of a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ac8b39e3-a9d0-56fd-8c0b-4d748bedf7d4" :question/math-academy-id "e-5926" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb46d056a8d8010eca509543c231c875f4980a21f1af17505fa98c8c64106207.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the graph of $y = \\dfrac{a}{x-b}+k.$ What is the value of $a+b+k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=-1,$ while the vertical asymptote is $x=2.$ This means that $k=-1$ and $b=2,$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{a}{x-2}+(-1) = \\dfrac{a}{x-2}-1.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(3,2)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x-2}-1 \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{a}{3-2}-1 \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+k = 3+2+(-1) = 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068655 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea2f1348-55bf-5313-8d5e-a5a097231e97" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a76e0252-0574-520e-bb5f-43c8faf6a564" :question/math-academy-id "e-8658" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y = \\dfrac{7}{2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $y = \\dfrac{7}{2x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e8/e80865b0f32a5473da27b39537034bcdabee0a6c24032f41413e20518642d3f4.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\dfrac{7}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\dfrac{7}{2x}.$\n\n![](images/b7/b7b1fe93de798c0aa91f60f66a2507869dbe837b843b7233972e1a78ee22576a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068656 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e11164-1929-594d-9f9e-460f6469421d" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Negative Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a18ff1e7-7f87-5cdd-9a25-91a2e9c1dd5b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8761" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y = -\\dfrac{1}{5x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $y = -\\dfrac{1}{5x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/d5/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\dfrac 1 5$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{5x}.$\n\n![](images/30/30ace3126ec127b9949ebf599d615020b9770458825d22460e9e7e0b3d5efec3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea2f1348-55bf-5313-8d5e-a5a097231e97" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a51b59f-8d07-510c-a5ca-9e6f34cd21ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6c7b719326bfa1a4b53fdf2bce3f6e7f1dafe5de2c994ffb4951a6d79af78707.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561614} {:answer/id #uuid "46916068-93c5-551e-ba98-d8c6ff2c7429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d7/d79bee1dd235ec65dd14b1c99702b078f91654465dbc68b62237b09636ea8fa3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561760} {:answer/id #uuid "66f9f632-8be5-5127-a9c2-07bcd823ccb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/19/1961fa6aebb1ea211272d37245cb96d6457fc26a30d1fc645d1edfdd7dc3a63d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561837} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8279b2-b0fa-5e46-ba0d-8e699e96db41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/04ca2ac857fb9f5083999f9d95bc6cb36bf10552fb12706a7ea8b86861c7bc5b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562094} {:answer/id #uuid "fd621ef5-df3a-5e58-9e19-4b5262a258de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0f/0fe642f3c7873344885b0e030fb449a8bf882120e675f18d72668ccae3ef4b40.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a51b59f-8d07-510c-a5ca-9e6f34cd21ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6c7b719326bfa1a4b53fdf2bce3f6e7f1dafe5de2c994ffb4951a6d79af78707.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561614} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc4317d-395a-50e5-9f31-626a8d8a2f94" :answer-field/key "selection" :ans