- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/a3/a32495fcca947d01cf8d3218fc5cfc0cce083a34e6fb6b629d92ba9e47039a6e.png)\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{4x}.$\n\n![](images/02/027b68fffd1555cc1735fc53a634684b019d396fd48bf7df9d430377ba56df21.png)\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units down to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{4x}-1.$\n\n![](images/e1/e1777e170fe23faa53a53a743ef9a6135451b2ed1b11762b146627790a6aacf8.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562443 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea2f1348-55bf-5313-8d5e-a5a097231e97" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ce3b216-d25a-50bd-ac4b-4fcef3d9d36d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/20/20395852a0e436d54029140fe79c4feadd9de30b091f744256b2e2e628d27725.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561621} {:answer/id #uuid "dccdf912-1bc2-5a7a-89a1-92d6f5513c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/344a3615421b88df05cb666ca90395991f3aa6af75c9095a60c73be89124b7e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562131} {:answer/id #uuid "e89981b3-8f60-53b0-adcd-cff91631be1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7f/7fff9c4bc90295cefb6f41880bcc903d1b4d418f8a470ec1a290bc030d37af8f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562157} {:answer/id #uuid "f93cdc66-9fba-5d2e-b1cb-b1094f30390f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9e/9e173bd5b4536c639f88f28e2600118f1acdcc4feb2f55db2439519572a32718.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562197} {:answer/id #uuid "fd180818-d83e-511f-80f7-41823befcdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e10be40920aebaaf2f5984e25cff2143ee145851d5feaef48df883cf3556cacc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd180818-d83e-511f-80f7-41823befcdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e10be40920aebaaf2f5984e25cff2143ee145851d5feaef48df883cf3556cacc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562206} :answer-field/id #uuid "e202ebbd-74b7-50fc-8387-e3cfbc2ec9ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71350d61-9672-52ac-9492-4bd38fc59f6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-99063" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{4}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $y=\\frac{4}{x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/b3/b3a79a8dbe82342c0ab1e16371f8c1d82833f4ebc3bad659f1a619ab1e92733e.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{4}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e1/e10be40920aebaaf2f5984e25cff2143ee145851d5feaef48df883cf3556cacc.png)"}]}
